{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 29, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "Arthur yawned, stretching in his familiar bed. Sunlight streamed through the window, just as it always did. But something felt…off. The colors seemed too vibrant, the details too sharp. He looked at his hand, noticing the perfectly rendered skin, the subtle texture of the skin pores. A notification popped up in his vision: \"Welcome, Arthur, to Aethelgard! Level 1 achieved.\" Panic seized him. He tried to reach for his phone, but his hand passed right through the nightstand. A nearby poster depicting a fantastical landscape shimmered, then solidified, becoming a real, three-dimensional archway. He was inside a video game. The realization crashed over him, a tidal wave of disbelief and terror.\n\n***\n\nHe stumbled out of his room, the house feeling strangely…constructed. The furniture was too perfect, the layout too symmetrical. A digital HUD overlaid his vision, displaying health, stamina, and a quest log filled with tasks like \"Gather 5 Wood\" and \"Defeat 3 Goblins.\" A cheerful, synthesized voice chirped in his ear, \"Greetings, Adventurer! Your journey begins now!\" Arthur stared at his reflection in a polished silver mirror, noticing his clothes had transformed into generic adventurer garb – leather tunic, sturdy boots, and a ridiculously oversized sword strapped to his back. He was no longer Arthur, accountant. He was a character, a pawn in someone else's digital world, and the thought sent a shiver of dread down his spine.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.16696929931640625}, {"token": "▁yawn", "logprob": -2.3997840881347656}, {"token": "ed", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -1.4305104514278355e-06}, {"token": "▁stretching", "logprob": -0.12137647718191147}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": -0.3717033565044403}, {"token": "▁his", "logprob": -0.05777266249060631}, {"token": "▁familiar", "logprob": -1.8159527778625488}, {"token"